# A slow version must be right whatever Link says, so it never has the typed operations: typed reads of elements, of fields, typed iteration and the calls of built-ins stay shut there, for some of them ask Link's tables about the contents of
# a list. What a slow version with a loop does have is the reckoning on what the walk has built in that very body: the counter is an integer, its remainder too; the read off the list is the closed read.
